  ],
  "text": " Just to explain the discrepancy between what\u2019s in the earlier messages and where you can find the data today: When the paper was released, we temporarily created a dataset in Data Explorer called \u201c NextGen Model Manuscript 2026 \u201d containing these new screens. \n However, since then we\u2019ve released the 26Q3 data, where the organoid lines have been processed with all other CRISPR screens. Since you can now find the new models in the harmonized CRISPR dataset, we\u2019ve removed the temporary dataset. See Yejie\u2019s message for how to find organoid data within CRISPRGeneEffect.csv (which is the name you can find under \u201cDownloads\u201d. This same data is labeled \u201cCRISPR (DepMap Public 26Q3+Score, Chronos)\u201d in Data Explorer) \n Thanks, \n Phil "
 },
